
Whereas,
a) The Lessor is owner of the property situated at D.No 7-1, China Amiram,
Bhimavaram, West Godavari District, A.P. State, India. Lessor constructed a building by obtaining permission from the concerned authorities.
b) The Lessee is engaged in the activities of Makers of Milkshakes and is in search of suitable premises for carrying on its business activities. The Lessee has approached the Lessor and requested a carpet area of 360 square feet.
c) The Lessor has offered to lease-out a shop on the Ground Floor (hereinafter referred to as the "Demised Premises") more particularly described in the schedule.
d)
The Lessee represents to the Lessor that he has the requisite permissions that are necessary for conducting the business from the concerned authorities.
e)
The Lessee has agreed to take on lease the Demised premises. Both the Lessor and the Lessee have mutually agreed to set out the terms and conditions of the lease as follows.
Now this lease deed witnesseth as follows:
1) The period of lease shall be for a period of Three(3) years commencing from 15-06-2023 and automatically coming to end on 14-06-2026.
2). The Lessee shall pay an amount of Rs.12000/- (Rupees Twelve Thousand Only) and GST. The GST or any future taxes on rentals on the Demised Premises will be paid by LESSEE only. The Lessee shall pay the Lease amount accordingly for every month on or before 10" day of every succeeding month after deducting TDS and shall deposit the same as detailed below:
仨
The electricity charges which will be paid by the Lessee only as per the consumption.
4)
The Lessee paid an amount of Rs.75000/- (Rupee Seventy Five Thousand Only) as an interest free refundable security deposit to the Lessor(SBI). UTR No:
317019744485, Bank: HDFC Bank, Date: 19/06/2023.
The Lessor shall refund the interest free refundable Security deposit to the Lessee upon the expiry or earliest termination of the lease agreement, whichever is earlier upon receiving back the vacant and peaceful possession of the Demised Premises and after satisfying themselves that all payments which have to be paid by the Lessee in regard to the Demised Premises and the services like electricity bill, water bill, etc.
6)
The Lessee shall enhance the lease amount by 5% every year over the rent period for the previous year.

7) The Lessor agrees to pay property taxes to China Amiram Gram Panchayat and all the other statutory payments, and the Lessce shall not be made liable for the
same.
8) The Lessee shall not use the demised premises for any other purposes other than the purpose for which it has been leased. Further the Lessee shall not sublease the Demised Premises during the lease period without the written consent of Lessor.
The Lessee shall not be allowed to SUBLEASE the Demised Premises.
The Lessee agrees to use the Demised Premises with due care & caution and shall keep and maintain the same in good condition. Minor day to day repairs of the Demised Premises will be the responsibility of the Lessee. The Lessee should not carry out any major additions or structural changes to the Demised Premises without the prior written consent of the Lessor and shall also abide by the rules and regulations of the concerned local authorities.
10) The Lessee agrees to pay all the expenses connected with lighting, maintenance, payable to them directly to the concerned person/authorities and shall furnish proof of payment to the Lessor on regular basis.
11) The Lessee has the right and shall be ailowed to display name board/sign board or the like at the front or outer elevation of the Demised Premises to the extent leased by Lessor.
12) Common toilet facility & maintenance of toilets will be borne by Lessor.
13) The Lessee shall neither carry nor stock any explosive materials alcohol or forbidden materials inside the demised premises and shall not carry out any activity in the demised building which is prohibited by Law of the Land.
14) That any dispute or discrepancies arising out of this agreement shall be subject to the jurisdiction of the courts at Bhimavaram, West Godavari Dist, A.P
15) The lease may be renewed at the option of the Lessor by giving two (2) months notice in writing in advance to the Lessee before expiry of the lease term.
However the said renewal, if any shail be on such terms and conditions as may be mutually agreed to by and between the Lessor and the Lessee in writing.
16) This Lease Deed shail be executed in duplicate. The original shall be retained by the Lessor and the duplicate by the Lessee.
17) The Lessee agrees to insure and to keep insured the demised premises against the loss or damages by fire, earthquake, riot or affray with a reputed insurance company and keep the Lessor indemnified from any loss including but not limiting to the actions of the Lessee.
18) The Lessor shall have a right to sell, assign or encumber the land during the subsistence of the lease period; and The Lessor shall have full right and authority to deal with the rest of the property in any manner.
19) The Lessee shall keep and maintain the Demised Premises in good, proper, and tenable condition at his own cost all the time during the lease period without causing any nuisance and disturbance to the neighbors.